# THE CLASS design.md Part 8 wart 20 states, and the half the poison cannot
# see (panel 177's item 2, route T; the compiler-engineer's E13): a copy made
# BEFORE the ending call still holds the old address, and `keep` was never
# ended through its own name, so neither the poison nor the checker's half
# knows anything about it. Before panel 177 this printed `-1`, the freed
# node's own word, at exit 0.
#
# What catches it is the DEAD SET: the runtime remembers the address
# `node_free` ended until C hands it out again, and the crossing into
# `node_value` finds it there. The pool never hands an address out twice, so
# the mark is still standing when the copy arrives; where C has reused the
# address first, the mark has been cleared and the copy is the documented
# limit `limit-a-copy-read-after-c-reused-its-address-is-not-caught` pins.

extern "dead-address-copy-made-before-the-end-reaches-c.h"
    record Node tag node
    function node_new() -> Node acquires node_free
    function node_free(n: Node consumes)
    function node_value(n: Node) -> i64

function main()
    a = node_new()
    keep = a
    node_free(n: a)
    print(node_value(n: keep))
